A||||7||theogre||Cave Update||||6||
Z||000000||theogre||11-29-2000||11:32 PM||||I've made a major change in how the left frame of the cave operates. I felt it was getting really long to scrol thru. (There are around 30 total pages in Tunnel 6 now. More are coming.)<P>The new menus will take you to a page as soon as you click on an item in the list.<P>If a menu is already showing a topic you want to go back to simply click GO below it.<P>The new menus are Java Script. They should work in all the reasonably current browsers. Let me know if you have problems. make sure you tell me what browser and version you are having trouble with.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Lake Superior? Is that what I stepped in? Sorry.||||reg||6
Z||000001||theogre||12-14-2000||09:08 PM||||I added a couple more pages and updated others. Will be another couple pages sometime in the next week. <A HREF="http://fierocave.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>The Fiero Cave</A><P>One important new page is on wiring in the ECM section. It lists potential source data for the various OE GM connectors. You can also go to Delphi's web site and get the whole connector catalog but it's a little tought to make sense of unless you are used to such things.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-15-2000||11:23 PM||||I did a small one today. Now if you add the cave to you favorites in IE5+ you'll get a nice little icon next to the short cut.<P>Someone asked me why I'm mainly dealing with IE now..... It's partly a matter of time. As many of you know this hasn't been the best year for me, I just don't have interest in the extensive testing I used to do. Since Netscape is now an AOHell property it's also fallen way behind in features. I'm trying to shift career gears a bit so I'm mainly interested in the more advanced new things. (Like the java scripted image map I'm working on for the DIS article.)<P>If you guys using netscape find a page you can't read let me know. I'll see what if anything I can do. I'm not trying to keep anyone out. Most of what I'm fooling with should work in the more recent NS version. I've tried to avoid specifically IE things but the Icon thing was one I couldn't resist.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever2||12-15-2000||11:30 PM||||For once I understood what you're talking about.  I have the icon now, and like it.<BR>I figured out that Ogre is the first letters of "<B>O Gre</B>at One".   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000004||theogre||12-24-2000||02:30 PM||||I added a couple more pages today.<P>An "improved" coolant filling procedure is in the engine area. It's mainly for people filling dry systems and systems where heater core work has been done.<P>My notes from fixing my radio last week are in the interior section. I'll add a diagram for the belt routing in the next week or so.<P>I also gave the little icon I mentioned above some road to drive on. The same Icon is used for both IE Favorites and Channels now.<P>I have <B>not</B> added all the new stuff to the channel. I'm not sure if I ever will. The channel is getting rather large. I haven't decided if I'll keep the off line channel support of dump it. Anyone have any thoughts? I figured it might give our traveling Fiero owners something to read on a long flight. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-24-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000005||Xtreme Fiero's||12-24-2000||08:44 PM||||none of the "GO" buttons work on my webtv, Is it a webtv problem (not compatible?) or what?||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||12-25-2000||02:46 PM||||I just checked them to make sure I didn't botch an update. Works ok in a browser.<P>Likely webTV doesn't fully support Java Script. Which would be no suprise. There's probly not much I can do about it. The number of articles is to long to go back to the old way. (There's over 30 now.) I'm working on something else but that uses an image map and may use java script as well. <P>Does the topic change when you select them from the list? It should. If that doesn't work either then it's a web TV problem. I'll have to think about what if anything will fix it. I'll look at microsofts specs for it next week. Knowing microsofts support of this product I don't expect much. If I can't find the info I need I'll see about a link to another frameset for you that won't use the scripts. That won't happen til sometime next week.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-25-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||12-26-2000||11:46 AM||||WebTV does have Java Script support. There are issues with it, especially on the older version of the hardware. It may be that tunnel 6 is to complex of a document for it or the "jellybean" java processing sytem doesn't support something in the scripts. I expect its the complexity since I'm not doing anything real advanced in that frame. there are however several scripts running at the same time.||||reg||1
